.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library defines the provider-neutral
.Dv org.5bsd.network
version
.Dv 1.0.0
interface.
Applications communicate with private or shared NetworkCmp instances through
brokered
.Xr libservice 3
channels.
No provider-specific networking structure is part of the public ABI.
.Pp
The
.Fn networkcmp_client_open
function consumes the local component channel that
.Xr serviced 8
injects through
.Ev NETWORKCMP .
The variable contains the decimal descriptor number; the descriptor itself is
the authority.
The common
.Xr libservice 3
helper validates the descriptor type and removes the variable from the
environment.
There is no global lookup or fallback path.
.Pp
Control operations use bounded messages with opaque, generation-tagged
handles.
.Fn networkcmp_hello
performs feature negotiation.
The library creates one process-wide, token-correlated client session,
performs the initial negotiation, and records the selected values.
Repeated opens return references to that same local authority.
The reply returned by
.Fn networkcmp_client_limits
is the binding contract for limits and negotiated features.
Negotiation occurs once at initial contact, not for each socket or packet.
Typed functions are provided for socket creation, bind, connect, listen,
accept, options, shutdown, close, and name resolution.
.Fn networkcmp_connect
starts a nonblocking connection and may return
.Er EINPROGRESS .
.Fn networkcmp_connect_status
polls completion without blocking and returns
.Er EINPROGRESS
while pending or the final socket error.
Callers impose their own deadline and cancel by closing the opaque socket.
.Fn networkcmp_accept
is nonblocking and returns
.Er EAGAIN
when no connection is queued.
.Fn networkcmp_send_inline
and
.Fn networkcmp_recv_inline
provide the universally available bounded data path for connected TCP and UDP
sockets.
Each operation transfers at most
.Dv NETWORKCMP_INLINE_MAX
bytes.
Send is nonblocking and may return a short stream write or
.Er EAGAIN .
Receive waits for at most
.Fa timeout_ms
milliseconds, where zero is a nonblocking poll.
The library implements the deadline with nonblocking provider requests;
the provider never sleeps on behalf of one request and can continue serving
other calls on the session.
It reports
.Dv NETWORKCMP_IO_F_EOF
for an orderly stream shutdown and
.Dv NETWORKCMP_IO_F_TRUNCATED
when a datagram exceeds the supplied capacity.
Connected UDP preserves one datagram per call.
.Fn networkcmp_resolve
implements bounded
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 Ns -style
forward resolution without exposing provider or resolver descriptors.
The caller supplies the result-array capacity through
.Fa nresults ;
on success it contains the number returned.
An optional canonical-name buffer and TTL output may be supplied.
A TTL of zero means the selected provider does not expose TTL information.
The base provider resolves independently of its socket RPC loop and permits
one active resolution per private component session.
An overlapping resolution fails with
.Er EBUSY .
.Fn networkcmp_getaddrinfo
is the familiar convenience interface.
It translates the bounded results into a linked
.Vt struct addrinfo
list and returns an
.Dv EAI_*
status.
The resulting list must be released with
.Fn networkcmp_freeaddrinfo ,
not
.Xr freeaddrinfo 3 .
Protocol and resolver failures return
.Li -1
and set
.Va errno .
.Pp
Typed operations are synchronous conveniences over asynchronous
.Xr libchannel 3
requests.
Kernel channel reply tokens correlate concurrent calls so threads cannot
consume one another's replies.
A reply acknowledges provider processing, not remote-host receipt.
Socket creation, connect, send, bind, accept, and shutdown are not
automatically replayed after an ambiguous channel failure.
The opaque client is process-bound.
The injected component session is retained as process-lifetime authority;
.Fn networkcmp_client_close
releases a library borrow, and a later
.Fn networkcmp_client_open
reacquires the same managed session without creating another channel reader.
If the provider returns a malformed typed reply, the library marks this
process-lifetime authority terminal.
The failing operation and every later operation return
.Er EPROTO
without sending another request, including after public close and reopen.
This fail-closed state prevents continued use of a provider that has violated
the negotiated protocol.
After
.Xr fork 2 ,
the child cannot reuse the parent's session and must open a separately
injected authority if one exists.
.Pp
Version 1 deliberately exposes only the bounded inline data path.
Any future bulk transport will use a separately negotiated protocol version
rather than reserving public structures and operations before their semantics
are implemented and tested.
.Pp
NetworkCmp transports bytes and datagrams only.
It does not open or save files and receives no filesystem capability.
An application that wants persistence reads from NetworkCmp and writes through
its independently injected FileSystemCmp.
The injected channel is non-transferable and locked against propagation
beyond the supervised exec.
.Pp
The
.Ql networkcmp
DTrace provider exposes component-open, message-send, message-receive, and
message-reject probes.
Provider daemons audit policy decisions through OpenBSM; client-library
activity is operational telemetry and is not audited.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr getaddrinfo 3 ,
.Xr libchannel 3 ,
.Xr libservice 3
